# L4 incremento 8 (docs/plans/l4-upgrade.md) — la DOMANDA INVERSA: la condizione
# come chiave. «Which verbs go before the subject when a bare verb follows?»
# legge la condizione con lo stesso lettore delle parti della lezione e risponde
# dalla stessa inverts_when_via/3 che la regola esegue, con il sostegno di
# ciascun verbo; lezione, analogia e ritiro la cambiano al turno dopo.

!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_LANG=en

[test la domanda inversa]
!timeout 8
> Which verbs go before the subject when a bare verb follows?
<~ None that I know
> A welder needs to wear a mask.
> To make a question with need, you can also put need before the subject when a bare verb follows.
> Which verbs go before the subject when a bare verb follows?
<~ «need» (you taught me that)
> Dare is an English verb lemma.
> "dares" behaves like "needs".
> A firefighter dares to enter a burning building.
> Which verbs go before the subject when a bare verb follows?
<~ «dare» (because it behaves like «need»)
> A welder needed to wear a mask.
> "dared" behaves like "needed".
> A firefighter dared to enter a burning building.
> To make a question with dare, you can also put dare before the subject in the past when a bare verb follows.
> Which verbs go before the subject in the past when a bare verb follows?
<~ «dare» (you taught me that)
<! need
> Which verbs go before the subject?
<~ and «need» only when a bare verb follows in the present (you taught me that)
> Quali verbi vanno prima del soggetto al passato quando segue un verbo nudo?
<~ «dare» (me l'hai insegnato tu)
> Forget that you can put need before the subject in a question.
> Which verbs go before the subject when a bare verb follows?
<~ None that I know

[test il file lascia la KB com'era]
!timeout 4
> forget that "dares" behaves like "needs"
> forget that "dared" behaves like "needed"
> Forget that you can put dare before the subject in a question.
> forget that dare is an English verb lemma
!reset
